!--- 3. Continuum frequency grid ---
! [OPT] MIN_CF raised: avoids sparse low-nu grid points that slow BA assembly
!        with minimal impact on IIn emission (peak flux well above 0.003x10^15 Hz)
! [OPT] MAX_CF lowered: 15.0 covers all relevant IIn continuum; cutting 20->15
!        removes ~15-20% of frequency points from the BA matrix
! [OPT] FRAC_SP / AMP_FAC tightened: smoother geometric spacing reduces
!        interpolation error in the Eddington factor iteration
! [OPT] MAX_BF tightened: better-resolved bound-free edges improve
!        the photoionization rates for the dominant O/Ne/Si species
! [OPT] V_CROSS / SIG_GAU_KMS coarsened: at VINF=10472 km/s the
!        thermal Doppler core is narrow; 1000 km/s spacing still resolves
!        line profiles while halving the number of explicit chi/eta points
